      "hints": [
        "For a right angle at $O$, set $\\overrightarrow{OA}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{OB}=0$.",
        "Only the second component contains $k$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$\\overrightarrow{OA}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{OB}=6(3)+(-2)k+(-6)(-3)=36-2k$.",
        "$36-2k=0$, so $k=18$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_id": "9709_s19_12_q8_ii",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "mapping": {
        "topic_id": "9709_p3_t_vectors",
        "lesson_id": "9709_p3_t_vectors_m01_l03"
      },
      "hints": [
        "Equal lengths give equal squared lengths.",
        "Keep both signs after taking the square root."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$|OA|^2=6^2+(-2)^2+(-6)^2=76$ and $|OB|^2=3^2+k^2+(-3)^2=18+k^2$.",
        "$76=18+k^2$, so $k^2=58$ and $k=\\pm\\sqrt{58}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_id": "9709_s19_12_q8_iii",
      "difficulty": 5,
      "mapping": {
        "topic_id": "9709_p3_t_vectors",
        "lesson_id": "9709_p3_t_vectors_m02_l01"
      },
      "hints": [
        "With $k=4$, $AC:CB=2:1$, so $\\overrightarrow{AC}=\\frac23\\overrightarrow{AB}$.",
        "Find $\\overrightarrow{OC}$ and divide by its magnitude."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$\\overrightarrow{AB}=(3,4,-3)-(6,-2,-6)=(-3,6,3)$, so $\\overrightarrow{AC}=\\frac23\\overrightarrow{AB}=(-2,4,2)$.",
        "$\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\overrightarrow{OA}+\\overrightarrow{AC}=(4,2,-4)$ and $|OC|=\\sqrt{16+4+16}=6$. The unit vector is $\\frac16(4,2,-4)$."
      ]
